        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. Employees shall be made aware of their vacation accruals on at least a monthly basis. Upon implementation of the University's automated accrual system, the University shall provide employees with at least sixty (60) calendar days notification that he/she will reach the maximum allowable accumulation.",
            "block_bbox": [
                183,
                153,
                1121,
                266
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    183.0,
                    153.0
                ],
                [
                    1121.0,
                    153.0
                ],
                [
                    1121.0,
                    266.0
                ],
                [
                    183.0,
                    266.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "2. The employee shall request dates for use of the vacation as soon as possible prior to the maximum accumulation. When the request is provided at least thirty (30) calendar days in advance, an employee shall be granted vacation before the employee's accumulated credit reaches the maximum, with the following exceptions:",
            "block_bbox": [
                180,
                290,
                1121,
                430
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    180.0,
                    290.0
                ],
                [
                    1121.0,
                    290.0
                ],
                [
                    1121.0,
                    430.0
                ],
                [
                    180.0,
                    430.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "a. If the specific dates on which the employee requests use of vacation credit cannot be granted, the employee shall be scheduled for alternate dates off; or",
            "block_bbox": [
                253,
                456,
                1120,
                540
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    253.0,
                    456.0
                ],
                [
                    1120.0,
                    456.0
                ],
                [
                    1120.0,
                    540.0
                ],
                [
                    253.0,
                    540.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "b. In the event the University cannot schedule alternate dates off, the vacation credit in excess of the employee's maximum allowable accumulation which cannot be used shall be placed in the employee's compensatory time bank and shall become compensatory time off credit.",
            "block_bbox": [
                253,
                567,
                1121,
                680
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    253.0,
                    567.0
                ],
                [
                    1121.0,
                    567.0
                ],
                [
                    1121.0,
                    680.0
                ],
                [
                    253.0,
                    680.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "3. In the event an employee fails to request use of vacation credit at least thirty (30) calendar days prior to reaching his/her vacation maximum, the University shall endeavor to grant the vacation use requested or schedule an alternate date.",
            "block_bbox": [
                181,
                704,
                1121,
                815
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    181.0,
                    704.0
                ],
                [
                    1121.0,
                    704.0
                ],
                [
                    1121.0,
                    815.0
                ],
                [
                    181.0,
                    815.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "If such request cannot be granted or an alternate date cannot be scheduled, and if the employee had been notified at least sixty (60) calendar days in advance that he/she was reaching the maximum vacation allowable, the vacation credit which would have taken the employee over his/her vacation credit maximum shall be lost to the employee.",
            "block_bbox": [
                252,
                842,
                1121,
                983
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
